<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plebeians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as plebeian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The plebeians were the body of ordinary Roman citizens, as distinct from the aristocratic patricians in the early Republic. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> they formed the broad citizen class below the senatorial and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/equites">equestrian orders</a>. Their status was above that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freedmen">freedmen</a> and the large enslaved population.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Plebeians</b> were at first excluded from the priesthoods; in principle the colleges were later opened to them.</blockquote><a href="/religion/roman-religion">Roman religion · Community &amp; Society</a></li></ul></section>
